{"name":"Blue Kelp","hex":"#1d7881","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"kelp","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several large brown algae seaweeds (especially of order Laminariales).","The calcined ashes of seaweed, formerly used in glass and iodine manufacture."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To gather kelp."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kelp"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kelp","blocks":[{"text":"Kelps are large brown algae or seaweeds that make up the order Laminariales. There are about 30 genera. Despite its appearance and use of photosynthesis in chloroplasts, kelp is not a plant but a stramenopile."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Kelp_In_Freycinet_Tasmania.jpg/330px-Kelp_In_Freycinet_Tasmania.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kelp"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Chowiet_Island_beach_kelp.jpg/500px-Chowiet_Island_beach_kelp.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Chowiet_Island_beach_kelp.jpg/1280px-Chowiet_Island_beach_kelp.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Chowiet_Island_beach_kelp.jpg/500px-Chowiet_Island_beach_kelp.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Alaskan beach kelp","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChowiet_Island_beach_kelp.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Five-ribbed_kelp_%28Costaria_costata%29.jpg/500px-Five-ribbed_kelp_%28Costaria_costata%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Five-ribbed_kelp_%28Costaria_costata%29.jpg/500px-Five-ribbed_kelp_%28Costaria_costata%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Costaria costata, five-ribbed kelp","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFive-ribbed_kelp_(Costaria_costata).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/KelpforestI2500ppx.JPG/500px-KelpforestI2500ppx.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/KelpforestI2500ppx.JPG/1280px-KelpforestI2500ppx.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/